{"duration_api_ms":8712,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"cebdfacf-7859-4c70-84fd-adac3a7b4abd","total_cost_usd":0.0578322,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4047,"cache_read_input_tokens":59861,"output_tokens":673,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4047,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":6,"outputTokens":673,"cacheReadInputTokens":59861,"cacheCreationInputTokens":4047,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0578322,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":4,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I implemented `to_cents` in `src/money.py`, and both tests in `tests.test_money` pass.\n\nIt turns the amount into a `Decimal` by way of `str(amount)`, multiplies by 100, and rounds half up. Going through the string matters because a float like `1.005` is really stored as `1.00499999…`. Plain float maths would round that down to 100 cents, but this version gives 101, which is what the test expects.\n\nThe trade-off is that the function rounds the shortest decimal form of the float (what Python prints for it), not its exact binary value.","ttft_ms":2237,"type":"result","duration_ms":8823,"uuid":"c619cea6-24f